<!--
UstaDesk : O'zbekcha (uz-UZ) WiX UI localization.

WiX v4.0.5 ships WixUI_*.wxl for ~35 cultures (ar-SA ... zh-TW) but there is no
Uzbek one, so this file supplies it. String Ids and the placeholder tokens
([ProductName], [1], [2], {\WixUI_Font_*}) match
WixToolset.UI.wixext 4.0.5 src/ext/UI/wixlib/WixUI_en-us.wxl one-for-one; only the
human-readable Value attributes are translated.

Not every dialog here is reachable from UstaDesk's installer: res/msi wires up
ui:WixUI Id="UI_MyInstallDialog" (Package/UI/MyInstallDlg.wxs) on top of
WixUI_Common, so the reachable flow is Welcome -> LicenseAgreement ->
MyInstallDirDlg -> VerifyReady -> Progress -> Exit, plus Cancel, Browse,
InvalidDir, FatalError, FilesInUse and the maintenance dialogs. The rest
(Advanced / Customize / Features / SetupType / InstallScope / OutOfDisk /
WaitForCosting) belong to dialog sets this project does not reference; they are
translated anyway so the file is complete and a culture fallback to English can
never leak into the wizard.

Untranslated on purpose: WixUI_Bmp_* / WixUI_Ico_* are resource names, and the
font sizes are numbers.

The apostrophe in o'/g' is ASCII (U+0027), matching src/lang/uz.rs, so the text
stays inside codepage 1252. Content is pure ASCII: no BOM, no XML declaration,
exactly like the en-us source.
-->
<WixLocalization Culture="uz-uz" Codepage="1252" xmlns="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxl">

